"type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":652,"digest":"sha256:2c4a87b384173803e0c94824473639090d1609d2c407b4a13b209b41f68095ff","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T19:39:28Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:39:28Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m125-v0.12.5/m12stage5-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m125-v0.12.5","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m125-v0.12.5","body":"# Engacer OS M12.5 / 0.12.5 — one Files environment\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE5-VM-v1**.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/evidence/M12/5/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n579 compiled Git inputs, ten native journeys, compact light/dark, twelve\ncached/full comparisons and matching VMware/BIOS install and independent starts.\nPublic release and full website proof close separately before M12.6.\n\nBuild: `69b114d97561bfe742ac9097748ad3d5`.\nISO SHA256: `36823e017ce466e0df39bcee5ad50b53eaa096f08ccaf4fb27165bac4a680fd7`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `27c9ae2fd336f5381e8972c36076c96053c09ccc8f0b886abaf5bff87e696b38`.\n\n## What changes\n\nOrdinary folders, the USB drive collection, USB folders and unavailable locations\nshare one frame. Back, Forward, Up, Refresh, address and Places remain in the same\npositions. Titles describe the actual provider. A narrow window replaces the\nsidebar with Places rather than hiding basic navigation. The Page controls are\nseparate from location history. Empty-state content fits short windows too.\n\nEach window keeps eight bounded location records including its provider, full\npath, item offset and USB generation-backed identity. Back does not mount a new\ndevice behind the user's back. A removed or replaced drive keeps its old location\nunavailable; choosing the connected drive explicitly opens its current contents.\nCtrl+N copies the real current location into an independent window.\n\nDrive objects select on one click and open on double-click or Enter. Ordinary\nUSB folders retain their actual FAT32 browsing and one-file create-only transfer\ncapabilities. Shared presentation does not invent unsupported filesystem actions.\nOptional USB addresses fit the full existing path without truncating its prefix.\nInvalid input keeps the previous location and remains editable for correction.\n\n[Architecture and decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/docs/architecture/files-m125.md),\n[Files guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/docs/handbook/files-m125.md),\n[eight-step installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/docs/handbook/install-m125.md).\n\n## Qualification boundary\n\nThe stage requires matching source/media, real setup and installed startup,\nordinary independent disk boots, its exact enabled-device VMware ZIP, separate\nBIOS journeys, actual 150%/4K frames, detach/replacement and independent stored\nbytes. Host history rules supplement these native observations. Managed pages,\nlinked fixed state and configured guest RAM are separate measurements.\n\nThe first complete candidate exposed root-breadcrumb/Refresh dispatch into an\nolder generic application handler. Its honest failure is retained. The corrected\nmedia repeated and passed its native and boot qualification before public closure.\n\nFile presentation, commands, dialogs and the other ordered desktop stages remain\nseparate. The shared-menu footer fitting and HiDPI cursor-versus-hit observation\nremain M12.14/M12.16 follow-ups. The earlier concurrent BIOS/AHCI timeout remains\nopen for M12.18; stress reliability is unqualified. Physical hardware, ARM,\nvendor GPU 3D and universal DOS/Windows compatibility are outside this stage.\nAgent visual/scenario review is not a human usability study.\n\nFixed shell state is **545,620 bytes**, **1,408 bytes** above M12.4 and\n**1,792 bytes** above M11.6. History/address storage accounts for that increase.\nTasks retain zero managed pages and no new allocation failures; idle CPUs halt.\nThe native main journey returns to 4,288,512 managed bytes after physical USB\ndetach. Framebuffer and device pages are measured separately. Font coverage\nremains 251,248 bytes; icon raster cache is zero. [Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/evidence/M12/5/resources.json).\n\n![Actual installed USB folder](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/bf68dd056c40348581ac99f28ff41b7acdd0e660/evidence/M12/5/feature.png)\n"}